  {
    "id": "casablanca-hassan-ii",
    "city": "Casablanca",
    "filename": "Framing Heritage - Hassan II Mosque.jpg",
    "source_page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Framing_Heritage_-_Hassan_II_Mosque.jpg",
    "download_url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/Framing_Heritage_-_Hassan_II_Mosque.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original",
    "author": "OussamaHamama",
    "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
    "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
    "location_evidence": "This image is the result of persistence rather than chance. Captured under the intense midday sun in August, it took numerous attempts to balance a handheld DSLR in one hand while positioning a wooden frame with the other. Looking through the optical viewfinder, I carefully adjusted focus, alignment, and perspective until the frame naturally embraced the Hassan II Mosque.\nEvery slight movement meant starting over. The final composition reflects the patience and precision often hidden behind a single photograph. More than a creative exercise, this image invites viewers to experience one of Morocco's most iconic landmarks from a different perspective, celebrating the country's rich architectural heritage and encouraging a deeper appreciation of its cultural legacy.",
    "source_width": 5184,
    "source_height": 3456,
    "alt": {
      "fr": "Mosquée Hassan II à Casablanca, vue à travers un cadre tenu par le photographe",
      "en": "Hassan II Mosque in Casablanca, seen through a frame held by the photographer"
